  "name": "Question 26",
  "problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{{2}^{z}}{\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}\\,\\text{d}z.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u={2}^{z}-9.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}z}={2}^{z}\\operatorname{ln}\u20612\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}\\,\\text{d}u={2}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{2}^{z}}{\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}\\cdot {2}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{1/2}}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
